# Bare `node_modules` / `dist` match only the repository root — Docker matches
# a pattern against the whole relative path, so `packages/*/node_modules` used
# to land in the build context and `COPY packages/<pkg>/ ...` then overwrote
# the pnpm install the builder had just done. The root `node_modules` IS
# excluded, so every nested symlink arrived dangling and the build failed on
# whatever a source file imported from a devDependency (slides' `ctx-spy.ts`
# imports `vitest`). CI never saw it, because a fresh checkout has neither
# directory — which meant the image could not be reproduced locally, and that
# is the capability whose absence let a broken image reach production.
**/node_modules
**/dist

.git
.harness-reports
*.actual.png
*.actual.html
